---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CTABlock from '../components/CTABlock.astro';

const milestones = [
  { year: '2006', note: 'Started in tech as a brand marketer at a small agency in Paris. Learned that most "strategy" decks died on contact with a real customer.' },
  { year: '2011', note: 'First real operating role. Discovered that shipping beats pitching, and that the shortest distance between a problem and a fix is usually a conversation, not a meeting.' },
  { year: '2014', note: 'First exit. Loud, messy, deeply educational. Promised myself the next one would be quieter.' },
  { year: '2018', note: 'Second exit. Quieter. Kept the promise.' },
  { year: '2021', note: 'Joined Tango as SVP Marketing. Built a team, a brand, and a lot of opinions about what "brand" means when nobody is buying from a banner anymore.' },
  { year: '2026', note: 'Stepping into fractional CEO, advisor, and coaching work. Fewer companies. Deeper with each.' },
];

const principles = [
  {
    title: 'Clarity before cleverness.',
    body: 'I would rather say the obvious thing first and be useful than say the interesting thing first and be impressive. Most founders are drowning in clever. They need a person who will tell them the obvious, out loud, once.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Story is strategy.',
    body: 'Every organization runs on a story. When the story is clear, the org chart feels like decoration. When the story fractures, no amount of process can paper over it. Most of my work is making the story honest again.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Two identities, one person.',
    body: 'I hold the operator and the human at the same time. The spreadsheet and the late-night conversation. People work with me because both show up. Not because I hide one to seem more serious.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Less, better.',
    body: 'I take on a small number of companies. I say no often. The work only compounds when there is room in my week to think about it, and yours, properly.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Stève Cattin"
  description="Fifteen years in B2B tech, two exits, and a genuine love for the obvious question nobody's asking."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="about-hero container">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="about-hero__title">
      Fifteen years in B2B tech.<br />
      Love asking <span class="accent">(obvious)</span> questions.
    </h1>
    <p class="about-hero__lede">
      Hi, I'm Stève. I help founders and senior leaders solve their challenges,
      with care, respect and curiosity. Marketer by training with a People &amp;
      Operations track record. Storyteller and advisor wherever I'm allowed.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- The Learning(s) -->
  <section class="about-body container-prose section-tight">
    <h2>The Learning(s)</h2>

    <p>
      When something isn't working, it's rarely just the plan. And it's rarely
      just the team. It's usually the space, the stories and the conversations
      between them. Where clarity breaks down, where ownership gets fuzzy, where
      smart people produce the wrong results anyway.
    </p>

    <p>
      I've spent most of my career working in those in-between spaces. Between
      the people building features and the customers paying for benefits – which
      is often the most expensive translation no one budgets for. Between
      American ambition and European execution. Between the strategy that makes
      sense on paper, the team that has to believe it enough to deliver it, and
      the operating system that makes the work progress.
    </p>

    <p>
      I'm drawn to people who are translating between worlds – a technical
      founder learning to be a storyteller, a marketer learning to run a P&amp;L,
      a CEO trying to build a company that matches who they actually are,
      rather than who they thought they were supposed to be.
    </p>

    <p>
      I've been lucky enough to do that work from the inside and lived through
      some very defining experiences: 2 acquisitions, building and scaling
      small-team Series A companies and also the difficult task of downsizing
      them, with care. From VC-funded startups in Switzerland, Fortune 500
      companies, and all the way to the executive leadership of a
      US-headquartered, PE-backed company. From Marketing to People, to
      Operations. From hands-on work with the team – aligning elements on a
      slide deck – to strategic conversations with my peers and the Board.
    </p>

    <p>
      Through it all, one constant: the better path is one made of curiosity,
      lack of ego and a genuine love for succeeding collectively rather than
      individually.
    </p>

    <h2>The Future</h2>

    <p>
      None of what I had the chance to experience was a given. I'm immensely
      grateful for each day, each person who entered my life, and each learning.
      Now I want to give back and see others benefit from it.
    </p>

    <p>
      The obvious next step after a seat at the executive table would be another
      seat at the executive table. That's not what pulls me. What gives me
      energy is the creative part – solving problems, and the quiet conversation
      with a leader about what's really going on. I also want the future to hold
      space for a personal dream that is close to my heart, and this is why a
      different path attracts me:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        I want to sit with founders and CEOs whose teams are stuck and who
        can't quite name why. Where the strategy looks fine on paper, the hires
        are good, and yet things aren't landing.
      </li>
      <li>
        Or with board members and investors whose portfolio companies are
        talented, well-funded, and somehow still slow. Sometimes the right
        intervention is a fractional operator. Sometimes it's an honest sparring
        partner for the founder.
      </li>
      <li>
        And with operators who sense that the hardest problem they're carrying
        is the one inside themselves, and need a sparring partner who's creating
        the safe space for them to share and work through it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Fewer companies than I could take. More depth with each.
    </p>

    <p>
      In a world where everything accelerates, I want to take the time to read
      what I'm given carefully – the doc, the deck, the org chart, the body
      language, the things people say after the meeting. I want to ask before I
      prescribe. Thorough and thoughtful by nature.
    </p>

    <p>If any of that resonates, reach out!</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Timeline -->
  <section class="about-timeline section container">
    <header class="about-timeline__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Path</p>
      <h2>Twenty years, compressed.</h2>
    </header>

    <ol class="about-timeline__list">
      {milestones.map((m) => (
        <li class="about-timeline__item">
          <span class="about-timeline__year">{m.year}</span>
          <p class="about-timeline__note">{m.note}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule" />

  <!-- Principles -->
  <section class="about-principles section container">
    <header class="about-principles__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">How I work</p>
      <h2>Four things I try not to forget.</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="about-principles__grid">
      {principles.map((p, i) => (
        <article class="about-principles__card">
          <span class="eyebrow eyebrow-amber">№ {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
          <h3>{p.title}</h3>
          <p>{p.body}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABlock
    id="book"
    eyebrow="If this resonates"
    headline="Let's have the conversation before anything else."
    body="A twenty-minute intro call. No deck, no pre-work. I'll ask what's actually going on. If the fit is real, we'll both know by the end."
    ctaLabel="Book an intro call"
    ctaHref="mailto:hello@stevecattin.com?subject=Intro%20call"
    secondaryLabel="Read some writing first"
    secondaryHref="/blog"
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* -------- Hero -------- */
  .about-hero {
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 4vw + 3rem, 7rem);
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .about-hero .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .about-hero__title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-hero);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .about-hero__title .accent {
    color: var(--color-cobalt);
  }

  .about-hero__lede {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: var(--lh-normal);
    color: var(--color-graphite);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  /* -------- Body -------- */
  .about-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }
  .about-body h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }

  .about-body p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: var(--lh-prose);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .about-body ul {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .about-body ul li {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: var(--lh-prose);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  /* -------- Timeline -------- */
  .about-timeline__header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .about-timeline__header h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-display);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  .about-timeline__list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .about-timeline__item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .about-timeline__item:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .about-timeline__year {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--color-cobalt);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-mono);
  }

  .about-timeline__note {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: var(--lh-normal);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  /* -------- Principles -------- */
  .about-principles__header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .about-principles__header h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-display);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  .about-principles__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .about-principles__card {
    background: var(--color-mist);
    padding: var(--space-8);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .about-principles__card h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .about-principles__card p {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: var(--lh-normal);
    color: var(--color-graphite);
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .about-timeline__item {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-2);
    }
    .about-principles__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
